{"format":"coupole-schema/1","id":"rayleigh_ciel","taille":[700,320],"titre":{"fr":"Pourquoi le ciel est bleu et le couchant rouge","en":"Why the sky is blue and sunsets red"},"alt":{"fr":"La lumière du Soleil traverse l'atmosphère ; les molécules diffusent surtout le bleu dans toutes les directions (ciel bleu). Au coucher, le trajet dans l'air est bien plus long : le bleu a été diffusé en route et la lumière directe arrive rouge-orangé.","en":"Sunlight crosses the atmosphere; molecules scatter mostly blue in all directions (blue sky). At sunset the path through air is much longer: blue has been scattered away and the direct light arrives orange-red."},"elements":[{"t":"arc","c":[350,520],"r":420,"a0":30,"a1":150,"style":{"trait":"terre","fond":null,"ep":3}},{"t":"arc","c":[350,520],"r":470,"a0":35,"a1":145,"style":{"trait":"eau","fond":null,"ep":1,"tirets":[5,4]}},{"t":"texte","p":[350,40],"txt":{"fr":"limite de l'atmosphère (épaisseur très exagérée)","en":"top of atmosphere (thickness much exaggerated)"},"taille":11,"ancre":"m","base":"milieu","couleur":"fin"},{"t":"point","p":[350.0,100.0],"r":5,"style":{"trait":null,"fond":"texte","ep":1.5}},{"t":"point","p":[608.58,189.04],"r":5,"style":{"trait":null,"fond":"texte","ep":1.5}},{"t":"texte","p":[350.0,118.0],"txt":{"fr":"midi : trajet court","en":"noon: short path"},"taille":12,"ancre":"m","base":"milieu","couleur":"texte"},{"t":"texte","p":[598.58,207.04],"txt":{"fr":"coucher : trajet long","en":"sunset: long path"},"taille":12,"ancre":"d","base":"milieu","couleur":"texte"},{"t":"ligne","p":[[350.0,20],[350.0,100.0]],"style":{"trait":"soleil","fond":null,"ep":2.5,"fleche":"fin"}},{"t":"ligne","p":[[797.7,336.79],[608.58,189.04]],"style":{"trait":"chaud","fond":null,"ep":2.5,"fleche":"fin"}},{"t":"ligne","p":[[350.0,60],[312.41,73.68]],"style":{"trait":"froid","fond":null,"ep":1.5,"fleche":"fin"}},{"t":"ligne","p":[[350.0,60],[330.0,94.64]],"style":{"trait":"froid","fond":null,"ep":1.5,"fleche":"fin"}},{"t":"lign